mac80211: minstrel_ht: keep a sample rate that is already in place

minstrel_ht_move_sample_rates() moves the sample rates that are still
valid to the front of the queue and returns how many there are. An entry
that was already in place was skipped without counting it, so the next
valid entry overwrote it and the count came up one short.

--- a/net/mac80211/rc80211_minstrel_ht.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rc80211_minstrel_ht.c
@@ -854,8 +854,11 @@ minstrel_ht_move_sample_rates(struct min
 			continue;
 		}
 
-		if (i == j)
+		/* already in place: keep it */
+		if (i == j) {
+			j++;
 			continue;
+		}
 
 		rates[j++] = cur;
 		rates[i] = 0;
